ate of pisupo (corned beef) and supoketi (spaghetti) served with white rice. A can of corned beef is in the background.","a":"Wyldephang","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","p":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=137749237"},{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Piula_Theological_College%2C_Upolu_island%2C_Samoa%2C_2009.jpg/960px-Piula_Theological_College%2C_Upolu_island%2C_Samoa%2C_2009.jpg","c":"Piula Theological College (Methodist) on the north coast of Upolu island in Samoa, 2009 The monastery is situated above a small cliff with steps leading down to the Piula Cave pool by the sea.","a":"Stephen Glauser","l":"CC BY-SA 2.0","p":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=8690692"},{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Samoa_fire_dance_-_siva_afi.jpg/960px-Samoa_fire_dance_-_siva_afi.jpg","c":"Boy performing a Samoa fire dance (siva afi) at a hotel in Apia.","a":"Neil","l":"CC BY 2.0","p":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=9406274"},{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Samoan_Siva_Tau.jpg/960px-Samoan_Siva_Tau.jpg","c":"Samoa performing their Siva Tau before playing South Africa at rugby union in the 2007 Rugby World Cup","a":"Fabienkhan","l":"CC BY-SA 2.0","p":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=2718133"},{"u":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Seumanutafa%27s_house_Apia_1896.jpg","c":"Samoan house Apia 1896. Correct name spelling should be 'Seumanutafa', but I've left the original photo description as it was published in the 1896 book.","a":"Charles S. Greene (1856-1930)Publisher: San Francisco news co. *uploaded by Tein","l":"Public domain","p":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=8522054"}]